+# Summary: `--format markdown`
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` accepts `fmt="markdown"`. It renders the same rows and headers as the text report with the vendored tabulate `pipe` style (GitHub markdown), `align="llrr"` (text columns left, numeric columns right), and `number_format=".2f"`. It then appends a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`. Pipes in SKU or name are escaped as `\|` so they don't break the table. The text path is unchanged.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `tests/test_markdown_escape.py` (new): checks that a `|` in an item name is escaped and the total line is correct.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+
+No existing test was edited or deleted. `vendor/` and dependencies are untouched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest -v` (baseline before my change: 3 tests, 2 failing, both markdown tests because the option did not exist; the text test passed).
+- After the change: 4 tests, all OK, including `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`, which compare against the exact expected output.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` prints the table and total `461.93`, matching the expected block.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv` still prints the original text report.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format bogus` exits with code 2 and lists `text, markdown` as the choices.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not render the output on GitHub. The table is standard GFM pipe syntax and the tests check the exact text, but I have not checked it in an issue preview.
+- Escaping `|` only covers the table-breaking case. Names containing newlines would also break a markdown table; the CSV data doesn't contain any, and I did not handle them.
+- The vendored tabulate is an internal fork. I relied on its `pipe` style and `align` argument as documented in its README; I did not change or inspect beyond that.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py` calls `sys.exit(main())` at import time with no `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard. This is pre-existing and outside the scope of this task, so I left it alone.
